---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { pathTo } from "../lib/paths.ts";
---

<BaseLayout title="About · Contribute Pulse" description="How Contribute Pulse ranks repositories, what the crawl includes, and how to fall off the board.">
  <article class="max-w-2xl">
    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl tracking-tight">About the board</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-moss">
      Contribute Pulse is a static discovery board for public GitHub repositories that are popular
      enough to matter, active enough that a pull request can actually get reviewed, and labeled
      enough that a new contributor has a place to start.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 font-display text-2xl">How scoring works</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-moss">
      Each listed repo gets a contribute score from 0–100. It is a weighted sum of five signals:
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-moss">
      <li><span class="text-ink">18% star band</span> — mid-size repos (about 300–15k stars) score highest. Mega-repos are penalized.</li>
      <li><span class="text-ink">28% freshness</span> — last push in the last week scores 100; older than 45 days is excluded.</li>
      <li><span class="text-ink">24% maintainer signal</span> — recent merged PRs, CONTRIBUTING.md, code of conduct, and a penalty if open PRs dwarf recent merges.</li>
      <li><span class="text-ink">20% issue quality</span> — starter-style issues that are recent, unassigned, and not already crowded with comments.</li>
      <li><span class="text-ink">10% project health</span> — license, topics, README, plus a weak forks/watchers signal.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-10 font-display text-2xl">Hard filters</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-moss">
      A repository is listed only if it is public, not archived, not a fork, has a license, has a
      description, has a default branch, was pushed in the last 45 days, has between 80 and 80,000
      stars (unless you turn on “Famous but hard”), and has at least one open issue labeled good
      first issue, help wanted, first-timers-only, beginner friendly, documentation, or
      hacktoberfest.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 font-display text-2xl">Caveats</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-moss">
      <li>Data is delayed up to 24 hours. The crawl runs daily at 02:00 UTC.</li>
      <li>Labels are imperfect. Maintainers reuse names, and GitHub search misses some of them.</li>
      <li>Always read the issue, contributing guide, and recent PR history before starting work.</li>
      <li>Category tags come from topics, language, and description keywords. Guessing is disclosed by also placing weak matches in Other.</li>
      <li>Merged-PR counts are sampled from the GraphQL API. When that sample is thin, maintainer activity is estimated from push recency.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-10 font-display text-2xl">How to get listed</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-moss">
      There is no submit form in v1. If a public repository matches the filters on the next daily
      crawl, it can appear. Topics, a license, a CONTRIBUTING.md, and a genuine starter issue help.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 font-display text-2xl">How to be excluded</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-moss">
      Archive the repository, remove the license, or go quiet for 45 days and it will drop off the
      next crawl. To request a removal from a current board snapshot, open an issue on
      <a class="text-lime hover:underline" href="https://github.com/csy20/contribute-pulse">the project repo</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-10 text-sm">
      <a class="text-lime hover:underline" href={pathTo("")}>Back to the board</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
